es'), but the codebase's closed strategy vocabulary is {static, jwt, introspection, proxy, custom} — 'jwks' is the verifier CLASS (JWKSTokenVerifier) backing the 'jwt' strategy, not a strategy token. A test parametrized over a literal 'jwks' strategy would exercise a strategy that AuthConfigError rejects as unknown.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd75a1fdbd37276de","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing (Unit middleware) and Acceptance Criteria bullet 3","norm_id":"nf85cabb988c1410f","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author writes a parametrized middleware-presence test using strategy='jwks' and it fails at server build with 'unknown auth strategy'","Reader of AC-3 tries to configure mcp.auth_strategies=['jwks'] and the server refuses to start"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Testing and AC-3, change 'static, jwks, proxy' to 'static, jwt, proxy' (the strategy tokens); optionally note that the SessionHintMiddleware wrap is unconditional so strategy choice does not affect its presence.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the \"bounded by distinct (principal, hint) pairs\" claim with the per-session hints the recipes recommend (${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID} / REBAR_SESSION_ID grow the pair-space unboundedly), and either state a retire/cleanup path for accumulating session-log pointers or quantify the growth and why it is acceptable.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"the server-side session-log pointer rotates per MCP identity instead of one shared log; the count is bounded by distinct (principal, hint) pairs ... no retire path is added (out of scope)\"","Client recipes bind the hint to a per-session id: \"headers: {\\\"X-Rebar-Session-Id\\\": \\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\\\"}\" and Codex \"env_http_headers = { \\\"X-Rebar-Session-Id\\\" = \\\"REBAR_SESSION_ID\\\" }\"","ABSENCE: with a per-session hint the (principal, hint) set is not bounded — it increases monotonically with session count, contradicting the \"bounded\" rationale on which the no-retire decision rests"],"finding":"The plan claims the server-side session-log pointer count is \"bounded by distinct (principal, hint) pairs\" and declares no retire path (out of scope), but the recommended hints are per-session identifiers (Claude Code's ${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}, Codex's REBAR_SESSION_ID), so the distinct (principal, hint) space grows with every new client session rather than being bounded. With no retire/cleanup path, session-log pointers accumulate unboundedly over the server's lifetime.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffc2fbeec96795e22","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Resolver consumers: \"session_log.py:58/151/184 ... the count is bounded by distinct (principal, hint) pairs ... no retire path is added (out of scope)\"","norm_id":"n9d89264556f091be","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the wrap ordering in mcp_server.py so the SessionHintMiddleware wrap and the existing ProxyAuthMiddleware wrap compose (each captures the prior `mcp.streamable_http_app` via a fresh `_orig_app` and reassigns), and note the intended outer/inner order.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'wired for every strategy by wrapping `mcp.streamable_http_app` with the proxy guard's method-assignment pattern (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:628-638`), unconditionally.'","mcp_server.py:628 `_orig_app = mcp.streamable_http_app` then :638 `mcp.streamable_http_app = _wrapped_streamable_http_app` — an in-place method reassignment that the new wrap must chain from, not overwrite.","The proxy wrap is gated on `auth_enabled and 'proxy' in mcp_cfg.auth_strategies`; the new wrap is unconditional, so under proxy both run and order matters."],"finding":"Under the `proxy` strategy the plan produces TWO sequential method-assignments to `mcp.streamable_http_app` (the existing ProxyAuthMiddleware wrap at mcp_server.py:628-638 and the new unconditional SessionHintMiddleware wrap), but does not specify their relative ordering or that each captures the other's result, so the second reassignment could clobber the first.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3761cd70509ca1e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Hint seam; Scope → src/rebar/mcp_server.py","norm_id":"nba3a287741878757","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deploying with the `proxy` auth strategy: if the SessionHint wrap re-reads `mcp.streamable_http_app` before the proxy wrap runs (or vice-versa without capturing `_orig_app`), one middleware is dropped from the ASGI stack — either the hint is never recorded or the proxy secret is never validated/stripped."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the SessionHintMiddleware wrap uses the SAME capture-then-reassign pattern applied AFTER the proxy block, reading the (possibly already-wrapped) `mcp.streamable_http_app` as its `_orig_app`, so under proxy the resulting stack is SessionHint(Proxy(streamable_http_app)).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"